%I A399326 #29 Nov 22 2026 21:32:34
%S A399326 2,13,23,83,17929,18121
%N A399326 Primes p such that the iteration of T(x) = x^2*(x^2 - 3)^2 collapses every element of GF(p) to 0.
%C A399326 Here V_3(x) = x*(x^2 - 3) = 2*T_3(x/2) is the monic Chebyshev (Dickson) polynomial of degree 3 and T(x) = V_3(x)^2.
%C A399326 For odd p > 3, T(x) == 0 (mod p) iff x == 0 or x^2 == 3, so 0 has a nonzero preimage iff Kronecker(3, p) = 1; hence every odd term satisfies p == +-1 (mod 12). The prime 2 is a term, while 3 is not.
%C A399326 T(1) = 4 and T(4) = 2704 = 16*13^2.
%C A399326 No other terms below 10^8 (exhaustive full functional-graph traversal of GF(p) for every prime p); a bounded-step orbit scan up to 2*10^9 found no further terms.
%H A399326 Igor M. Zhuk, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23420627">Unital Collapse Primes in Arithmetic Dynamics: Total Backward-Orbit Collapse for T(x) = (x^2 - 2)^2 mod p, Galois Stratification, and Fermat-Totient Asymptotics</a>, Zenodo preprint (2026).
%H A399326 Igor M. Zhuk, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23856837">Total-Collapse Primes of Polynomial Maps over GF(p): Eighteen Families and Two Related Sequences</a>, Zenodo preprint (2026); <a href="https://github.com/Nondual-Observer/total-collapse-primes-oeis">GitHub verification suite</a>.
%F A399326 p is in the sequence iff #{x in {0..p-1} : T^(p)(x) == 0 (mod p)} = p, where T(x) = x^2*(x^2 - 3)^2 mod p and T^(k) denotes the k-th iterate of T.
%e A399326 For p = 2: T(0) = 0, T(1) = 4 == 0 (mod 2), so all 2 elements of GF(2) reach 0 in 1 step; thus 2 is in the sequence.
%e A399326 For p = 13: T(0) = 0, and T(4) = 16*13^2 == 0 (mod 13), with all 13 elements of GF(13) reaching 0 within 4 steps; thus 13 is in the sequence.
%e A399326 For p = 23: all 23 elements of GF(23) reach 0 within 8 steps under iteration of x^2*(x^2 - 3)^2 mod 23; thus 23 is in the sequence.
%o A399326 (Julia)
%o A399326 using Primes
%o A399326 function isok(p::Int)
%o A399326     (!isprime(p) || (p > 2 && !(p % 12 in (1, 11)))) && return false
%o A399326     f(c) = mod(mod(c * mod(c*c - 3, p), p)^2, p)
%o A399326     st = zeros(UInt8, p); st[1] = 2
%o A399326     for x in 1:(p >> 1)
%o A399326         st[x + 1] == 2 && continue
%o A399326         c = x; while st[c + 1] == 0; st[c + 1] = 1; c = f(c); end
%o A399326         st[c + 1] == 1 && return false
%o A399326         c = x; while st[c + 1] == 1; st[c + 1] = st[p - c + 1] = 2; c = f(c); end
%o A399326     end
%o A399326     return true
%o A399326 end
%o A399326 println(filter(isok, primes(2, 20000)))
%Y A399326 Cf. A019434, A401173. See the linked article for the companion sequence for V_9(x)^2.
%K A399326 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399326 1,1
%A A399326 _Igor Zhuk_, Nov 16 2026
